    "x": 0,
    "y": 1
   },
   "id": 2,
   "options": {
    "content": "### Credit rate card (no currency)\n\nRelative units, no currency anywhere. 1 credit = 10k Sonnet-input-equivalent tokens. Rates mirror the RATIOS the vendor publishes between models (Opus 5x Sonnet; output 5x input), so a credit means the same thing on every dashboard whatever the vendor charges this month. Cache reads weigh a tenth, cache creation a quarter more, as the vendor ratios do.\n\n| tier | credits per 1k input | per 1k output |\n|---|---|---|\n| faq | 0.0 | 0.0 |\n| engine | 0.0 | 0.0 |\n| search | 0.05 | 0.0 |\n| nav-sonnet | 0.3 | 1.5 |\n| nav-opus | 1.5 | 7.5 |\n| none | 0.0 | 0.0 |\n| cache read | x0.1 of input | |\n| cache creation | x1.25 of input | |\n| search_call (flat) | 2.0 | |\n| engine_step (flat) | 0.0 | |\n| faq_hit (flat) | 0.0 | |\n\nA navigator answer costs 20–30 credits; a FAQ hit and an engine step cost nothing; a semantic search costs 2.",
    "mode": "markdown"
   },
   "title": "Rate card",
   "type": "text"
  },
  {
   "datasource": {
    "type": "prometheus",
    "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
   },
   "fieldConfig": {
    "defaults": {},
    "overrides": []
   },
   "gridPos": {
    "h": 6,
    "w": 6,
    "x": 12,
    "y": 1
   },
   "id": 3,
   "options": {
    "colorMode": "value",
    "graphMode": "none",
    "reduceOptions": {
     "calcs": [
      "lastNotNull"
     ],
     "fields": "",
     "values": false
    }
   },
